      "math_academy_id": "q-128433",
      "knowledge_point_id": "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors",
      "problem": "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨0,-1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,9,2⟩,$ and $c=⟨2,7,6⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}9 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+(3\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 2)+4(3\\cdot 7-2\\cdot 9) \\\\  & =14+12 \\\\  & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|26|=26.\n$$",
