      "knowledge_point": "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar",
      "problem": "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨0,3,6⟩$, $q=⟨t,t,2⟩$, and $r=⟨-1,2,7⟩$ are coplanar.",
      "worked_solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ t & t & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & 2 \\\\ -1 & 7\\end{aligned}|+6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}t & t \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-3(t\\cdot 7-(-1)\\cdot 2)+6(t\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot t) \\\\  & =-21t-6+12t+6t \\\\  & =-3t-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ -3t-6 & =0 \\\\ -3t & =6 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=-2.$",
